{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "testrunner",
      "runtimeExecutable": "go",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "-C",
        "tools/testrunner",
        "run",
        "./cmd/testrunner"
      ],
      "port": 8799
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server",
      "runtimeExecutable": "pnpm",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server-seam",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "pnpm",
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567
    },
    {
      "name": "game-server-platform",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "GGD_PLATFORM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "GGD_WHITELIST_BYPASS=1",
        "pnpm",
        "--filter",
        "@ggd/game-server",
        "dev"
      ],
      "port": 2567,
      "comment": "game-server that can actually reach a LOCAL platform (the built-in default is the k8s host `platform:8080`, which never resolves on a dev box, so combat-env/curation always fail safe). Whitelist stays bypassed so the default-empty curation list cannot filter the roster to zero."
    },
    {
      "name": "platform",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "DATA_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/data",
        "CONTENT_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/content",
        "REDIS_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6379",
        "PLATFORM_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080",
        "JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=devsecret",
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "GAME_SERVER_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:2567",
        "PLATFORM_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "GGD_DEPLOY_TIER=private",
        "go",
        "-C",
        "apps/platform",
        "run",
        "./cmd/platform"
      ],
      "port": 8080
    },
    {
      "name": "platform-invite",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "DATA_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/data-invite",
        "CONTENT_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/content",
        "REDIS_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6379",
        "PLATFORM_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080",
        "JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=devsecret",
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=devseam",
        "GAME_SERVER_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:2567",
        "PLATFORM_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080",
        "GGD_DEPLOY_TIER=private",
        "GGD_REQUIRE_INVITE=1",
        "GGD_REGISTER_RATE_LIMIT=20",
        "go",
        "-C",
        "apps/platform",
        "run",
        "./cmd/platform"
      ],
      "port": 8080,
      "comment": "task #174: the FAMILY-BUILD posture of the same platform — registration requires an invite code minted in the admin console (邀請碼). The plain `platform` entry stays open because it binds loopback (see config.resolveRequireInvite); this entry is what the deploy actually runs. Its own DATA_DIR so exercising the gate never writes into the dev store. Add GGD_OWNER_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=1 on a real deploy to close the first-account window too."
    },
    {
      "name": "redis-attack",
      "runtimeExecutable": "redis-server",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "--port",
        "6390",
        "--bind",
        "127.0.0.1",
        "--save",
        "",
        "--appendonly",
        "no"
      ],
      "port": 6390,
      "comment": "#174 ADVERSARIAL REVIEW ONLY. A throwaway loopback-bound Redis so an attack instance of the platform cannot collide with (or pollute) the shared dev platform's keyspace on 6379 — idx:username / bootstrap:owner are global, and the review has to race the first-account window. Never used by a real deploy."
    },
    {
      "name": "platform-invite-attack",
      "runtimeExecutable": "env",
      "runtimeArgs": [
        "DATA_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/data-invite-attack",
        "CONTENT_DIR=/Users/Takuro/GGD/content",
        "REDIS_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6390",
        "REDIS_PASSWORD=d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e5a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f9",
        "PLATFORM_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8091",
        "JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=a7f3c1e9d24b8065fe1a3c7b90d5e2846bb17c40aa93d5e6f80217c4d3b9e51a",
        "PLATFORM_GAME_SHARED_SECRET=8c1d0f2ab649e3577d0c9b1e4a86f2350ed7c9b1a24f68d035ce7a19b4620fd8",
        "GAME_SERVER_ADDR=http://127.0.0.1:2567",
        "PLATFORM_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8091",
        "GGD_DEPLOY_TIER=private",
        "go",
        "-C",
        "apps/platform",
        "run",
        "./cmd/platform"
      ],
      "port": 8091,
      "comment": "#174 ADVERSARIAL REVIEW ONLY. Gated posture on its own port + DATA_DIR + Redis so the attack run never touches the shared dev platform another agent is using on 8080. GGD_REQUIRE_INVITE is deliberately UNSET and the bind is 0.0.0.0 — the run therefore exercises the DEFAULT derivation (non-loopback ⇒ gated), which is the posture a real deploy would land in. Rate limit is off so a throttle cannot be mistaken for the gate holding. Real (non-dev) secrets because the deployed-secret guard refuses to boot a non-loopback bind on dev defaults."
    },
    {
